.TH ELEPHANTWALK 1
.SH NAME
elephantwalk \- walk a rocking elephant about the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/elephantwalk
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ElephantWalk
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Games/ElephantWalk.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The elephant is a single sprite, and the whole of the demonstration is
the one line that draws it:
.IP
.EX
Sprite3ZB(gr.dc,x,y,0,$IB,"<1>",BI=1$,Sin(8*tS)/4);
.EE
.PP
.IR Sprite3ZB 's
last argument is a rotation about z in radians, so the elephant is
tilted by up to about fourteen degrees either way each time it is
drawn, and the original's loop blocks waiting for a key \- so that is
once per step.
The elephant rocks as it walks.
.PP
The rotation is about the sprite's own origin rather than the middle of
its bitmap.
The bin's rectangle is (\-124,\-100)\-(95,136), which puts the origin
near the elephant's shoulder, and that is what it pivots around.
.PP
The elephant faces the other way while it is walking right \- the
original sets
.B DCF_SYMMETRY
only when x has increased, so a vertical step clears it again.
Steps are 32 pixels and walk off one edge and back on at the other.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "arrows / wasd"
.TP
.B arrows / wasd
Walk 32 pixels
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TF /icons/temple/elephantwalk_1.bit
.TP
.B /icons/temple/elephantwalk_1.bit
the sprite, from the bin in ElephantWalk.HC
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/elephantwalk.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR elephant (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original redraws only when a key arrives, so the rock is sampled
once a step rather than animated continuously, and this follows it.
A free-running version would look smoother and would not be the same
program.
.PP
There is no window border, no
.B WinMax
and no
.BR AutoComplete ;
the panel is a fixed 500 by 360 and the wrap is at its edges rather
than the screen's.
